{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0122Qf7YDXTH695Ltx9mEJdp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: xling-calib-direction-writing\n3\tdescription: Writing and visual presentation patterns from 8 papers on cross-lingual calibration and representations\n4\ttype: skill\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# Cross-Lingual Calibration — Writing Patterns (8 papers)\n8\t\n9\t## Narrative\n10\t\n11\t**Story type**: \"突破局限型\" (7/8). Blind spot → reveal → fill. High conf.\n12\t\n13\t**Intro**: 4 paragraphs (5/8). P1 motivation → P2 prior work → P3 gap+approach → P4 three contributions [(1) discovery, (2) method, (3) generalization]. High conf.\n14\t\n15\t**Hooks** (pick one):\n16\t- English-centric gap: \"Prior work focuses on English, leaving X unexplored\" (xiao, zhou). 2/8.\n17\t- Name the meta-problem: \"Square One Bias\" (zhou) — forces acknowledgment.\n18\t- Cognitive dissonance: \"LLMs are surprisingly well-calibrated\" (joshi) — contradicts expectation.\n19\t- Pain narrowing: \"most dangerous hallucination — confident wrong answers\" (ji).\n20\t\n21\t**Tension**: Show standard practice actively fails, not just untried. \"Fine-tuning doesn't change alignment\" (liu). \"Final layer overwrites multilingual signals\" (zhou). \"Aggregate correlation masks instance-level failure\" (ravisankar). 3/8. High conf.\n22\t\n23\t## Insight Delivery\n24\t\n25\t**Layer-wise revelation** (3/8): Probe all layers → phase transition → motivates method. Signature move of this subfield.\n26\t\n27\t**Negative-as-evidence** (2/8): \"X doesn't work\" proves your design. SAE failure → distributed signal → justifies probe (miao2026coral). SFT doesn't align → explicit alignment needed (liu).\n28\t\n29\t**\"Finding the knob\"** (ji): Abstract concept → manipulable direction. Provides understanding + intervention.\n30\t\n31\t## Figures\n32\t\n33\t**Figure 1**: 50/50 motivation (analytical) vs method overview (method papers). High conf.\n34\t\n35\t**Layer analysis → line plots** (universal). Overlay conditions on same axes. Never tables for continuous layer data. High conf.\n36\t\n37\t**Xling transfer → heatmaps**. Side-by-side at contrasting layers (xiao: layer 3 vs 19). 3/8.\n38\t\n39\t**Gain highlighting**: Dashed baseline line (miao2026coral), before/after panels (xiao), curve gaps (ji). 4/8.\n40\t\n41\t**Progression**: motivation → method → finding → ablation → surprise. 14+ figures: front-load key results, appendix for per-language. 6/8.\n42\t\n43\t## Tables\n44\t\n45\t**Main result**: rows=methods, cols=datasets×metrics, grouped by dataset. Bold best. 3-4 baselines main, full in appendix. 5/8. High conf.\n46\t\n47\t**Ablations**: full numbers (8/8). No checkmark grids. Delta-from-base rare. High conf.\n48\t\n49\t**Division**: Continuous → figures. Discrete comparisons → tables. Per-language → appendix. Mechanistic = figure-heavy; benchmarking = table-heavy. High conf.\n50\t\n51\t**Appendix**: Main 1-2 models + key langs. Appendix exhaustive. zhou: 15 main, 122 appendix. 6/8.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63663d37-a323-4180-9c6d-c85faa2f45aa","uuid":"7d9575ec-21f8-4e57-9db1-613d26ffaf99","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:27:32.505Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/skills/projects/xling_calib_direction/distilled-writing.skill.md","content":"---\nname: xling-calib-direction-writing\ndescription: Writing and visual presentation patterns from 8 papers on cross-lingual calibration and representations\ntype: skill\n---\n\n# Cross-Lingual Calibration — Writing Patterns (8 papers)\n\n## Narrative\n\n**Story type**: \"突破局限型\" (7/8). Blind spot → reveal → fill. High conf.\n\n**Intro**: 4 paragraphs (5/8). P1 motivation → P2 prior work → P3 gap+approach → P4 three contributions [(1) discovery, (2) method, (3) generalization]. High conf.\n\n**Hooks** (pick one):\n- English-centric gap: \"Prior work focuses on English, leaving X unexplored\" (xiao, zhou). 2/8.\n- Name the meta-problem: \"Square One Bias\" (zhou) — forces acknowledgment.\n- Cognitive dissonance: \"LLMs are surprisingly well-calibrated\" (joshi) — contradicts expectation.\n- Pain narrowing: \"most dangerous hallucination — confident wrong answers\" (ji).\n\n**Tension**: Show standard practice actively fails, not just untried. \"Fine-tuning doesn't change alignment\" (liu). \"Final layer overwrites multilingual signals\" (zhou). \"Aggregate correlation masks instance-level failure\" (ravisankar). 3/8. High conf.\n\n## Insight Delivery\n\n**Layer-wise revelation** (3/8): Probe all layers → phase transition → motivates method. Signature move of this subfield.\n\n**Negative-as-evidence** (2/8): \"X doesn't work\" proves your design. SAE failure → distributed signal → justifies probe (miao2026coral). SFT doesn't align → explicit alignment needed (liu).\n\n**\"Finding the knob\"** (ji): Abstract concept → manipulable direction. Provides understanding + intervention.\n\n## Figures\n\n**Figure 1**: 50/50 motivation (analytical) vs method overview (method papers). High conf.\n\n**Layer analysis → line plots** (universal). Overlay conditions on same axes. Never tables for continuous layer data. High conf.\n\n**Xling transfer → heatmaps**. Side-by-side at contrasting layers (xiao: layer 3 vs 19). 3/8.\n\n**Gain highlighting**: Dashed baseline line (miao2026coral), before/after panels (xiao), curve gaps (ji). 4/8.\n\n**Progression**: motivation → method → finding → ablation → surprise. 14+ figures: front-load key results, appendix for per-language. 6/8.\n\n## Tables\n\n**Main result**: rows=methods, cols=datasets×metrics, grouped by dataset. Bold best. 3-4 baselines main, full in appendix. 5/8. High conf.\n\n**Ablations**: full numbers (8/8). No checkmark grids. Delta-from-base rare. High conf.\n\n**Division**: Continuous → figures. Discrete comparisons → tables. Per-language → appendix. Mechanistic = figure-heavy; benchmarking = table-heavy. High conf.\n\n**Appendix**: Main 1-2 models + key langs. Appendix exhaustive. zhou: 15 main, 122 appendix. 6/8.\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
